WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.395
Here is the estimator workflow, reproduced
with an anonymized saved

00:00:04.395 --> 00:00:08.441
estimate. The fifteen thousand dollars is a
CMS cost allowance.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:13.295
It is not the itemized Control System
calculation, and it does not

00:00:13.295 --> 00:00:15.318
increase automatically with pixel count.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:21.092
The estimator now identifies that allowance
and links to Control System.

00:00:21.092 --> 00:00:25.312
Open it, then search under Load from an
estimated job.

00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:29.955
The saved-job connection is fixed: this
example loads both LED displays

00:00:29.955 --> 00:00:35.441
at their actual pixel sizes. The TV is
excluded from LED pixel sizing.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.061
To check the reported scale separately, here
are two test displays

00:00:41.061 --> 00:00:44.341
totaling thirteen point eight two four
million pixels.

00:00:44.341 --> 00:00:48.442
These are test dimensions, not confirmed as
Matt's original inputs.

00:00:48.442 --> 00:00:52.132
Review live video, outdoor, sports venue,
professional stadium, and

00:00:52.132 --> 00:00:54.183
software license settings before building.

00:00:55.283 --> 00:00:59.905
Select Build estimate. The Control System
now shows an itemized package

00:00:59.905 --> 00:01:02.847
using Jackson's existing rules and catalog
prices.

00:01:02.847 --> 00:01:07.048
This test configuration comes to two hundred
eighteen thousand, three

00:01:07.048 --> 00:01:10.830
hundred ninety-six dollars and twenty-six
cents in selling price.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:15.032
That is a test result, not an approved job
quote.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:20.140
Review the equipment quantities, costs,
margins, and selling prices.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:23.244
Export Excel to keep the full breakdown.

00:01:23.244 --> 00:01:28.121
This is the calculated CMS package to
review, rather than treating

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:31.668
the estimator's fifteen-thousand-dollar
allowance as the finished Control

00:01:31.668 --> 00:01:32.555
System price.

00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:37.270
Processing is separate. The processing
section still states that it

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:41.216
carries no price, so this is not a complete
processing quote.

00:01:41.216 --> 00:01:45.521
The confirmed fix is the saved-job
connection and the clear route from

00:01:45.521 --> 00:01:48.390
the estimator allowance to the calculated
CMS breakdown.
